  "build_note": "The PyPI sdist is the python-libfyaml directory of the libfyaml v1.0.0-rc2 tag but lacks the C library its setup.py builds from the repository root, so the image pins both, checks that the sdist's Python package, setup.py and LICENSE are identical to the tag's python-libfyaml, and installs from the tag tree: setup.py builds the bundled static libfyaml with CMake (clang -O0 and LLVM source coverage passed through its documented LIBFYAML_CMAKE_ARGS) and links it into _libfyaml.abi3.so. All PyPI releases of the binding are pre-releases (1.0.0a1 to 1.0.0rc2); the latest is pinned (taoJSON pre-release precedent). The official wheels are not installed.",
  "dependencies_note": "No Python runtime dependencies; setuptools and wheel are build backend only; libfyaml is linked statically.",
  "parser_family": "libfyaml 1.0.0-rc2 (C scanner/parser and generic value builder) through the python-libfyaml _libfyaml extension; same family as the C cell libfyaml path (0.9.6)",
